/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  chemistry/HTart-formation.dat -- the first dissociation of tartaric acid,
  written from the neutral master:   H2Tart  <=>  HTart- + H+

  logK25 = -pK1 = -3.036 and dH = +3.19 kJ/mol are the selected values of
  Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231, Table 7.63
  (L-(+)-tartaric acid), p. 347, reaction (1): pK 3.036, dG 17.330 kJ/mol,
  dH 3.19 kJ/mol, dCp -147 J/mol/K at 298.15 K and I = 0 (evaluation grade ABA).
  The independent measurement, Patterson & Woolley, J. Chem. Thermodyn. 33 (2001)
  1567-1585, Tables 9 and 10, agrees: pK 3.0360, dH 3.10 kJ/mol.

  CORRECTED 2026-11-12 (C372; the architect's authorisation).  This record used to carry
  logK -2.98 and dH +3.8 kJ/mol: the pK was an uncited handbook value ("literature,
  25 C"), 0.056 below the evaluated one, and the dH was the difference of two formation
  enthalpies of Kochergina et al. (2006).  The ionisation ENTHALPY now comes from
  Goldberg, not from Kochergina's hfAq: the two differ by -0.61 kJ/mol (Goldberg 3.19 minus
  Kochergina-derived 3.8), inside Kochergina's +/-1.5 per species.  The species' hfAq
  (species/HTart.dat) stay Kochergina's.

  Hand-curated organic chemistry -- NOT from the PHREEQC inorganic import that
  supplies most of this directory.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType aqueousSpeciation;
schemaVersion 1;

species HTart; masters ( { ion H2Tart; nu 1; } { ion H; nu -1; } );
      logK25 -3.036; dH 3190; source "Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231, Table 7.63, p. 347: pK1 3.036, dH1 +3.19 kJ/mol (298.15 K, I = 0); agreeing measurement Patterson & Woolley, J. Chem. Thermodyn. 33 (2001) 1567, Table 9";
